Imports:
  - Types:
      - Exchange
    From: freqtrade/exchange
  - Types:
      - IStrategy
    From: freqtrade/strategy
  - Types:
      - IPairList
    From: freqtrade/plugins/pairlist
  - Types:
      - IProtection
    From: freqtrade/plugins/protections

Usages:
  dynamic_loading: |
    All resolvers except `ExchangeResolver` locate a concrete subclass by scanning Python files
    under a standard search path (project user_data/<subdir>, then a built-in fallback
    directory) for a class named object_name that subclasses object_type, then instantiate
    it with keyword arguments. `ExchangeResolver` instead looks up the class by name directly
    on the freqtrade.exchange module namespace, since exchange subclasses ship with freqtrade
    itself rather than being user-authored.

Annotations: |
  This cell is freqtrade's generic dynamic-class-loading mechanism: given a name (from config
  or CLI) and an expected base type, find and instantiate the matching class. `plugins/
  pairlist`, plugins/protections, strategy, and exchange are all "pluggable" precisely
  because this cell can load any of their concrete subclasses by name at runtime.

  Use `dynamic_loading` to understand how a name in config becomes a live instance.

---

"IResolver()":
  location: iresolver.py
  annotations: |
    Base class for name-to-class dynamic loading. Concrete resolvers set the class attributes
    object_type (the expected base class) and object_type_str/user_subdir/extra_path
    (used to build the search path), then reuse the methods below unless they need custom
    lookup logic.
  methods:
    "build_search_paths(config: dict[str, Any], user_subdir: str | None, extra_dirs: list[str] | None) -> paths:list[str]": |
      Compute the ordered list of directories to scan for a matching class.

      Algorithm:
      1. Start from the built-in fallback directory for object_type
      2. Prepend the user's user_data/<user_subdir> directory, if configured
      3. Prepend any `extra_dirs` (e.g. a strategy's own strategy_path setting)
    "load_object(object_name: str, config: dict[str, Any], kwargs: dict[str, Any], extra_dir: str | None) -> instance:Any": |
      Find the class named object_name under object_type on the computed search paths and
      instantiate it with `kwargs`.

      `instance`: constructed object; raises OperationalException if not found
    "search_all_objects(config: dict[str, Any], enum_failed: bool, recursive: bool) -> objects:list[dict[str, Any]]": |
      Enumerate every class matching object_type found on the search paths, without
      instantiating them (used for list-strategies-style commands).

      `enum_failed`: include modules that failed to import, with their error, instead of
      silently skipping them

"IResolver::ExchangeResolver()":
  location: exchange_resolver.py
  annotations: |
    Resolves exchange names directly against the freqtrade.exchange module namespace rather
    than scanning the filesystem, since all exchange subclasses ship with freqtrade; see
    `dynamic_loading`.
  methods:
    "load_exchange(config: dict[str, Any], exchange_config: dict[str, Any] | None, validate: bool, load_leverage_tiers: bool) -> exchange:Exchange": |
      Instantiate the `Exchange` subclass matching `config`'s exchange id.

"IResolver::StrategyResolver()":
  location: strategy_resolver.py
  annotations: |
    Resolves a user-authored strategy class by name.
  methods:
    "load_strategy(config: dict[str, Any] | None) -> strategy:IStrategy": |
      Find and instantiate the `IStrategy` subclass named in config["strategy"].

"IResolver::PairListResolver()":
  location: pairlist_resolver.py
  annotations: |
    Resolves a pairlist/filter handler class by name.
  methods:
    "load_pairlist(pairlist_name: str, exchange: Exchange, pairlistmanager: Any, config: dict[str, Any], pairlistconfig: dict[str, Any], pairlist_pos: int) -> pairlist:IPairList": |
      Find and instantiate the `IPairList` subclass named `pairlist_name`.

"IResolver::ProtectionResolver()":
  location: protection_resolver.py
  annotations: |
    Resolves a risk-control handler class by name.
  methods:
    "load_protection(protection_name: str, config: dict[str, Any], protection_config: dict[str, Any]) -> protection:IProtection": |
      Find and instantiate the `IProtection` subclass named `protection_name`.

---

Author: Goga
CreatedAt: 25/08/26
Description: |
  Generic dynamic-class-loading mechanism behind every "pluggable" cell (exchange, strategy,
  pairlist, protection). Other concrete resolvers not documented here (`HyperOptLossResolver`,
  `FreqaiModelResolver`) follow the same `IResolver` pattern for the un-scoped optimize/
  hyperopt and freqai subsystems.
